  "generated_text": " $ $p(x) = ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d$ for some constants $a,$ $b,$ $c,$ and $d.$  Then\n\\[p(n) = an^3 + bn^2 + cn + d = \\frac{1}{n^2}.\\]Setting $n = 1, 2, 3,$ and $4,$ we get the system of equations\n\\begin{align*}\na + b + c + d &= 1, \\\\\n8a + 4b + 2c + d &= \\frac{1}{4}, \\\\\n27a + 9b + 3c + d &= \\frac{1}{9}, \\\\\n64a + 16b + 4c + d &= \\frac{1}{16}.\n\\end{align*}Solving this system, we find that $a = -\\frac{1}{60}, b = \\frac{1}{6}, c = -\\frac{1}{2},$ and $d = .$.$ Therefore, $p(5) = \\frac{1}{25}.$The answer is: \\frac{1}{25}",
  "grade": {
